      "problem": "Find the exact value of ${cos}^{2}⁡({75}^{∘})-{sin}^{2}⁡({75}^{∘}).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={75}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡({75}^{∘})-{sin}^{2}⁡({75}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {75}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡{150}^{∘} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
